From u8bb087a769327765 at groups.google.com  Tue May 16 00:07:31 2017
From: u8bb087a769327765 at groups.google.com (Kelly J Iknayan)
Date: Tue, 16 May 2017 00:07:31 +0000
Subject: Importance of Effective Sample Size
Message-ID: <4sirCFY6a0U.hkKtx7k6AQAJ@hmecology.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/hmecology/c/4sirCFY6a0U/m/hkKtx7k6AQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi All,

In ecological literature, I have not noticed much attention paid to the effective sample size of posterior distributions (except maybe in Bayesian phylogenetic analyses).

As a first question, should ESS be evaluated/reported with analyses using MCMC? I'm a bit muddled on its importance in comparison to convergence diagnostics and/or MC error.

As a corollary, is there any rule of thumb for sufficient ESS?

For reference, here are some of the recommendations I’ve come across.

 “[F]or many purposes it should suffice to have 100 or even 10 independent simulation draws”.  Gelman et al. (2014, p 287) <https://books.google.com/books?hl=en&lr=&id=ZXL6AQAAQBAJ&oi=fnd&pg=PP1&ots=uOYkx-hC0-&sig=mVXpBoMw9WxkFsXAw3P9Dhu9r-Q#v=onepage&q&f=false>
More than a “very short effective sample”. Kéryand Royle (2015, p 65) <https://books.google.com/books?hl=en&lr=&id=B_mcBAAAQBAJ&oi=fnd&pg=PP1&dq=Applied+Hierarchical+Modeling+in+Ecology&ots=FR3HMZxA6r&sig=AXWhKsGPVrw7uAfYYcXIe7GcsvI#v=onepage&q=Applied%20Hierarchical%20Modeling%20in%20Ecology&f=false>
 >10000. Recommended on a blog post by John K.Kruschke <http://doingbayesiandataanalysis.blogspot.com/2016/07/mcmc-effective-sample-size-for.html>
~4000. For high-dimensional settings. Gong and Flegal (2016, p 697) <http://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/10618600.2015.1044092>
Estimation of the minimum multivariate ESS; depends on the number of model parameters (Vats et al. 2015 <https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.07713>; R package mcmcse; and here <https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/49570/effective-sample-size-for-posterior-inference-from-mcmc-sampling>)

Thanks in advance for the help,

Kelly
